# PIXELTRUTH Project Memory

## Project intent

PIXELTRUTH is a local-first Python 3.11 + Streamlit image metadata inspection and digital forensics application. It must report explainable evidence and limitations, not certify authenticity or manipulation.

## Durable decisions from the supplied master prompt

- Target macOS and Windows; use free/open-source Python dependencies and no paid APIs or compulsory cloud services.
- Keep core analysis independent from Streamlit where practical.
- Supported initial formats: JPEG/JPG, PNG, WEBP, TIFF, BMP, GIF. Optional HEIC/HEIF is future work.
- Hash the exact uploaded bytes with SHA-256.
- GPS is hidden until explicit user action and excluded from reports by default.
- ELA is JPEG-only; histograms are descriptive; missing metadata alone is not proof of manipulation.
- Assessment labels are LOW CONCERN, NEEDS REVIEW, and INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE. No REAL/FAKE labels or authenticity percentages.
- No permanent image storage by default; do not automatically upload, log image contents, or expose internal paths.
- requirements.txt is the dependency source of truth. Do not install packages until the relevant phase is authorized.
- Development is gated by explicit START PHASE 0 through START PHASE 5 commands. Stop and report after each authorized phase.

