- Phase 1 verification: 29 Pytest tests passed after recheck; pip check reports no broken requirements; AppTest script execution passed; local Streamlit health endpoint returned 200. Recheck fixed valid EXIF orientation labels incorrectly marked Invalid and marks palette image bit depth unavailable when it cannot be stated reliably. No packages were installed during Phase 1.
- Phase 1 limits at completion: XMP/IPTC parsing was marked Unsupported; GPS, integrity findings, comparison, ELA, histograms, assessment, and PDF output were not implemented yet. Phase 2 has since added integrity findings, GPS, and comparison.
- Phase 2 is complete on develop. Added core/metadata_integrity.py, core/metadata_consistency.py, core/gps.py, and core/comparison.py; extended EXIF fields for timestamps and stored pixel dimensions; added MetadataField source-grouped display, GPS reveal/clear controls, and two-image comparison UI. A later metadata-support extension adds core/xmp.py and core/iptc.py without changing the shared metadata model.
- Phase 2 verification after the metadata-support extension: 57 Pytest tests passed, covering GPS parsing for JPEG/PNG/WEBP/TIFF, XMP and IPTC locations, malformed inputs, privacy separation, and comparison. pip check and git diff check passed; local Streamlit health and page endpoints returned 200. AppTest timed out on a later repeat in this environment. No packages were installed.
- Phase 2 limits: GPS is not included in normal inspection results. XMP supports JPEG APP1, PNG `XML:com.adobe.xmp` text chunks, WebP `XMP ` RIFF chunks, and TIFF tag 700; IPTC supports JPEG Photoshop APP13 `8BIM` 0x0404 and TIFF tag 33723. JPEG Extended XMP is detected but not reassembled; other storage locations/formats are not parsed. XMP packets with DTD/entity declarations are rejected. Pixel similarity is a bounded descriptive mean-absolute-difference indicator, not SSIM or an authenticity score. Phase 3 assessment, ELA, and histograms are not implemented.

## Next required context

Next phase: wait for explicit START PHASE 3 authorization before implementing assessment logic, JPEG ELA, and RGB histograms. Do not treat Phase 2 findings as an authenticity verdict.

## Update rule

Update this file after every completed development phase with decisions, implementation status, test results, and remaining issues. Do not record a phase as complete until phases.in exit criteria are satisfied.
